From: Jonathan Roth <jr@462eng.fr>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:30:00 +0200
Subject: native: Forget hot-unplugged secondary GPUs

MetaBackendNative only listened to udev "add" events: when a secondary
DRM device went away, MetaKms merely re-probed it (failing with "Failed
to reopen") and the MetaGpuKms / MetaKmsDevice stayed around forever.
This had two consequences:

 * the kernel may hand the same /dev/dri/cardN to a new device, which is
   then rejected by on_udev_device_added() ("device already present"),
   while the stale MetaKmsImplDevice may even reopen the new node by
   path;
 * the DRM lease manager never saw the device go away, so the
   wp_drm_lease_device_v1 global was never removed and Xwayland kept the
   DRM fd it received through the drm_fd event. That fd keeps the
   removed drm_device alive, its minor is never freed, and every
   hotplug cycle (e.g. DisplayLink/evdi) consumes a new cardN until the
   64 primary minors are exhausted.

On udev "remove" of a non-primary GPU's node, remove the GPU from the
backend, remove its MetaKmsDevice from MetaKms (closing it and marking
it so it never reopens its path), let the DRM lease manager withdraw
the device from Wayland clients through a new MetaKms::device-removed
signal, and drop the remaining references once the renderer no longer
uses the GPU.

Bug: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/issues/710
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-28

